WEBVTT

00:00:00.792 --> 00:00:01.501
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.437 --> 00:00:06.162
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s somebody who shows you round a city or a museum.

00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:08.901
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.480
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s something which we use to pay, instead of cash.

00:00:15.494 --> 00:00:16.266
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:22.532
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s somewhere where people go when they want to send a parcel or a letter.

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:25.364
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:27.966
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s a kind of fruit.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.445
It’s long and yellow.

00:00:32.478 --> 00:00:33.361
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.834
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s the opposite of <i>expensive</i>.

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:39.667
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:40.631 --> 00:00:44.028
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s a like sweater, but it has buttons.

00:00:46.092 --> 00:00:46.874
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.981
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s similar to a wallet, but it’s also for coins.

00:00:54.037 --> 00:00:54.686
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

00:00:55.599 --> 00:00:56.653
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It’s a verb.

00:00:57.258 --> 00:01:02.396
For example, you do this to the TV when you’ve finished watching something.